from pathlib import Path
import csv,json,hashlib
src=Path('reviews/darkmatter-2026-10-13/round6/snapshots/h1_final/results')
dest=Path('reproducibility/darkmatter/round7_analyses/h2_context/H1_COMPLETENESS.md')
read=lambda n:list(csv.DictReader((src/n).open(),delimiter='\t'))
models=read('v3_pgls_model_summary.tsv');sens=read('v3_pgls_sensitivity.tsv');c=json.loads((src/'v3_closure_verification.json').read_text());meta=read('v3_comparator_metadata_summary.tsv')[0]
lines=['# H1 completeness and result audit','', 'Generated by `reviews/darkmatter-2026-10-13/round7/root_checks/generate_h1_summary.py` directly from the authoritative round6 `h1_final` result tables. This replaces an inaccurate hand-transcribed summary; the original is retained in round7/snapshots/h2_initial. No underlying H1 analysis was changed.','', 'The primary PGLS covers all 237 Thermoplasmatota genomes. Seven model specifications comprise the primary S1 and six sensitivity models S2–S7. Slurm job53704703 completed successfully. Existing numerical verification against statsmodels supports reusing these results without a redundant rerun, subject to the scientific bounds below.','', '## Primary and OLS coefficients','', '| Variable | PGLS coefficient | PGLS SE | PGLS p | OLS coefficient | OLS SE | OLS p |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in models:lines.append('| '+' | '.join(x[k] for k in ['variable','pgls_coef','pgls_se_unb','pgls_pval_unb','ols_coef','ols_se_unb','ols_pval_unb'])+' |')
lines+=['','## All model specifications','','| Specification | n | Lambda | AAI coefficient | AAI SE | AAI p | RBH coefficient | RBH SE | RBH p | GLS R² |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in sens:lines.append('| '+' | '.join(x[k] for k in ['model_id','n','lambda_ml','coef_aai','se_unb_aai','p_unb_aai','coef_frac_rbh','se_unb_frac_rbh','p_unb_frac_rbh','r2_gls'])+' |')
lines+=['','## Numerical verification','',f"Primary lambda: {c['primary_lambda_ml']}; profile interval: {c['primary_lambda_ci95']}. Primary GLS R²: {c['primary_r2_gls']}; OLS R²: {c['ols_r2']}. Maximum absolute statsmodels discrepancies: coefficient {c['max_abs_diff_vs_statsmodels_beta']}, SE {c['max_abs_diff_vs_statsmodels_se']}, R² {c['max_abs_diff_vs_statsmodels_r2']}. These are implementation checks, not proof of model assumptions.",'','## Comparator and caller scope','',f"The {meta['n_genomes']} genome-comparator pairs use {meta['n_unique_nearest_comparators']} unique external accessions. Of the pairs, {meta['n_nearest_gtdb_r232_rep']} use GTDB references and {meta['n_nearest_mgnify']} use MGnify; {meta['n_biome_soil']} are labelled soil, {meta['n_biome_marine_sediment']} marine sediment and {meta['n_biome_unannotated_gtdb_only']} have unknown environmental metadata. Pair counts must not be presented as counts of unique comparator genomes.",'', 'The five genomes missing archived CheckM2 FAA inputs for the S7 complete-gene proxy are: '+', '.join(c['missing_checkm2_faa_genomes'])+'. S7 contains232 genomes. Catalogue/metagenomic and CheckM2/single-genome gene-call bases differ; denominator and completeness-proxy sensitivities do not remove all caller effects.','','## Interpretation and placement','', 'Higher AAI and lower shared-RBH coverage are conditional associations in the multivariable model. Do not interpret the AAI coefficient as a positive marginal relationship, or describe the two sets of proteins as disjoint components. The results do not demonstrate accessory expansion, ancestral gain/loss, horizontal transfer, de novo gene birth, cultivation status effects, or an explanation for all between-phylum darkness differences.','', 'The 237 genomes are the enumerated study cohort. PGLS intervals and tests are model-based and conditional on the selected phylogeny/covariance specification; coefficient intervals are conditional on fitted lambda unless explicitly stated otherwise. Profile-lambda and covariance/rooting checks do not propagate topology or branch-length uncertainty. High lambda is evidence of residual phylogenetic covariance under this model, not a percentage of darkness explained or proof that vertical history dominates all other explanations.','', 'A short within-Thermoplasmatota result can fit the main text, with model tables and diagnostics in the supplement. Final placement remains subject to Argon review. Public-data/deposition gaps from prior rounds remain separate from internal reproducibility.','','## Source hashes','']
for fn in ['v3_pgls_model_summary.tsv','v3_pgls_sensitivity.tsv','v3_closure_verification.json','v3_comparator_metadata_summary.tsv']:
 lines.append(f'- `{fn}`: `{hashlib.sha256((src/fn).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}`')
dest.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print(dest)
